Subject: a token log takes a valid token issued before the first it checked
Why: Quiver's simulation of its persisted class (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 6, AC-T2.2.5) replays a run from its seed: the log refused a valid token issued before the first it checked, and tokens carry their issue time in whole seconds of the wall clock, so whether a run's tokens straddled a second decided whether a server refused one, and a tenth of the seeds ran apart across processes; in production a client with a valid token went unvalidated. Offered upstream on cp/t2.2-token-log (20cdaf9)

